   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Jairo,<div><br></div><div>Many thanks for your reply.</div><div>Yes, you are right. My &quot;ms3.out&quot; folder has been generated. I just started to learn R studio and I am making pre-testing analysis with the data that I collected from myself before my real data collection. Therefore, I am not so experienced and I could not solve this problem. How can I generate this folder? What should I do? If you share your ideas with me, I will be so grateful to you.</div><div><br></div><div>Regards,</div><div>Canan<br><br>23 Mart 2020 Pazartesi 09:34:09 UTC tarihinde Jairo Hidalgo Migueles yazdı:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Canan,<div>Can you check if your &quot;ms3.out&quot; folder has the meta data of the first of your raw files? It seems it was not generated.</div><div>Best,<br>Jairo<br><br>El domingo, 22 de marzo de 2020, 1:20:07 (UTC+1), canan yüksel  escribió:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">Dear all,\r\n\r\nI am taking this error message and I could not understand what is the problem.How can I solve this problem? I am just learning how to use GENEActiv data; therefore, I could not understand what the problem is. Could you help me about that, please?\r\n\r\nRegards\r\n\r\nCanan\r\n\r\nPart 4\r\n 1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in readChar(con, 5L, useBytes = TRUE) : cannot open the connection\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">In addition: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Warning message:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">In readChar(con, 5L, useBytes = TRUE) :\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> cannot open compressed file &#39;C:/output1/output_Data/meta/ms3.out/NA&#39;, probable reason &#39;No such file or directory&#39;\r\n\r\n<p>I used this example code:</p><p>(I am using this code in the data that I downloaded directly from the GENEActiv device as a cvs file.)</p><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">\r\n</span><div><pre style=\"background-color:rgb(247,247,247);border-bottom-left-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-top:0px;overflow:visible;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:10px;padding-right:10px;padding-top:10px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><code><a style=\"color:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;text-decoration:inherit\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">library</span>(GGIR)</a>\r\n<a style=\"color:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;text-decoration:inherit\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">g.shell.GGIR</span>(</a>\r\n<a style=\"color:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;text-decoration:inherit\" rel=\"nofollow\">             <span style=\"color:rgb(144,32,0)\">mode=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">c</span>(<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">2</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">3</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">4</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(64,160,112)\">5</span>),</a>\r\n<a style=\"color:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;text-decoration:inherit\" rel=\"nofollow\">             <span style=\"color:rgb(144,32,0)\">datadir=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(64,112,160)\">&quot;C:/mystudy/mydata&quot;</span>,</a>\r\n<a style=\"color:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;text-decoration:inherit\" rel=\"nofol